    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "42cdff21_224d5228",
        "filename": "Documentation/filesystems/incfs.rst",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 16,
      "author": {
        "id": 1080076
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-16T07:25:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Android has to run with the previous kernel, and should run with the one from the next release. We can\u0027t update R anymore, not this kind of updates at least. This basically locks the API in its current shape for several releases",
      "parentUuid": "67164947_603006ca",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 16,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 16,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "93eb31b2b7173eb451fc7356340059577601d825",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6d981a28_833aedc9",
        "filename": "Documentation/filesystems/incfs.rst",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 37,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125653
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-16T05:50:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "sysfs is \"one value per file\", which is not this 😞\n\nIf you want multiple values, use debugfs.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 37,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 37,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "93eb31b2b7173eb451fc7356340059577601d825",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "63db9192_578ef7da",
        "filename": "Documentation/filesystems/incfs.rst",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 37,
      "author": {
        "id": 1080076
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-16T06:56:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Android doesn\u0027t mount debugfs in user builds anymore. Also, this is one value - a value of the last error that happened on the filesystem. It can\u0027t be split into separate files as reading them isn\u0027t atomic and will produce bogus results when the error changes",
      "parentUuid": "6d981a28_833aedc9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 37,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 37,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "93eb31b2b7173eb451fc7356340059577601d825",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "222f6c3d_61517b78",
        "filename": "Documentation/filesystems/incfs.rst",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 37,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125653
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-16T07:05:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "why do you need to know this on a userbuild?\n\nAnd this is not \"one value\" is it something that you have to parse.  It feels like this is a debugging thing.",
      "parentUuid": "63db9192_578ef7da",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 37,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 37,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "93eb31b2b7173eb451fc7356340059577601d825",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "70a62225_ce8dba2f",
        "filename": "Documentation/filesystems/incfs.rst",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 37,
      "author": {
        "id": 1080076
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-16T07:10:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This isn\u0027t actually a debugging feature, but a part of the metrics Play needs to collect for the streaming installation monitoring and optimization. It is currently already collecting the read logs from files installed on IncFS, but read logs aren\u0027t produced in case of read error, and they don\u0027t carry the error code. This value would let Play monitor the quality of the streaming nuggets they produce, and optimize them on the fly",
      "parentUuid": "222f6c3d_61517b78",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 37,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 37,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "93eb31b2b7173eb451fc7356340059577601d825",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2a15a288_a038fddf",
        "filename": "Documentation/filesystems/incfs.rst",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 37,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125653
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-16T07:17:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\"last error\" is crazy to be relying on sysfs for.\n\nJust use a proper kernel trace for something like this if you really rely on it, this is not what sysfs is for and you will end up missing events.",
      "parentUuid": "70a62225_ce8dba2f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 37,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 37,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "93eb31b2b7173eb451fc7356340059577601d825",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0b4d44fe_8f63ddea",
        "filename": "Documentation/filesystems/incfs.rst",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 37,
      "author": {
        "id": 1080076
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-16T07:25:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What is that proper trace we could use? Is it as lightweight as sysfs?\n\nBTW, it\u0027s totally fine to lose events here, all it needs is to return a consistent \"last error\" event that happened at the moment of polling. This gets joined later with the app crash / lag / ANR metrics to determine if we can connect it to the app being streamed",
      "parentUuid": "2a15a288_a038fddf",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 37,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 37,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "93eb31b2b7173eb451fc7356340059577601d825",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "77ade595_aa34c78b",
        "filename": "Documentation/filesystems/incfs.rst",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 37,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125653
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-16T08:49:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "sysfs should not be used for error-passing of kernel issues to userspace, as you will drop events and there is lots of other issues.  Please use a \"proper\" api for stuff like this.",
      "parentUuid": "0b4d44fe_8f63ddea",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 37,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 37,
        "endChar": 17
